= Sublingual immunotherapy side effect management

It is common and normal to feel an itchy mouth or throat when starting the tree, grass, ragweed, or dust mite tablets. It is the natural allergic response to the allergen in the tablet.

Your body will get used to the allergen after a few weeks and the side effects will decrease naturally as you desensitize. If the side effects are bothersome before that occurs, here are tips to help your body adapt to the medication.

Side effect:
- Bothersome itchy mouth or discomfort (mild) - sucking on an ice cube or popsicle can help
- Bothersome itchy mouth or discomfort (moderate) - Break tablet in half and only take half tab per day for 2 weeks before trying the full one again AND/OR give a non-drowsy antihistamine 1 hour before the dose for 2 weeks, then try without
- Bothersome itchy throat or discomfort (mild/moderate) - hold dose udner tongue for 1 minute then spit. Do this for 2 weeks then go back to swallowing after the 1 minute. AND/OR break the tablet in half etc. 2 weeks, AND/OR give a non-drowsy antihistamine 1hr before for 2 weeks, etc.
- Lump under the tongue: quarter per day 2 weeks, then half x 2 weeks, then full as tolerated

Any of the strategies can be combined and donea t the same time. The steps can also be trialled for longer than 2 weeks. The key is to try and continue the emdicien in some way if possible, to allow your body time to build tolerance to the allergen.

If despite trying the above symptoms are still bothersome, please contact the clinic.
